Subject: [PATCH 07/10] Resolve a queue drop's neighbour in core

Both apps found the row after a drop among the rows they had loaded and
sent it as the entry the moved row goes before, so a drop just before a
row not read yet moved nothing. The reorder command now takes the moved
entry, its lane and the place among the lane's rows it goes to, and core
reads the row it then sits before in SQL. Android tracks the held row's
place by the list's own step offsets instead of searching its rows by key.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019wwAR9dZVZXyrPK4PqBSPW
